<!--
    decbench: a short-circuit boolean assignment stays an explicit 0/1 diamond.
      Case: O0-bash-bash-time_command  (docs/decbench/triage/)

    Source (gcc -O0 -fno-pie -c), the exact idiom the triage case reduces to:

        int f(int *p, int q)
        {
          int x = p && (p[1] & 0x100);
          return x * 2 + q;
        }

    gcc materializes the boolean as a jump-based select whose `mov $0,%eax`
    arm is the SHARED target of every short-circuit exit:

        0:  endbr64 ; push %rbp ; mov %rsp,%rbp
        8:  mov %rdi,-0x18(%rbp) ; mov %esi,-0x1c(%rbp)
        f:  cmpq $0x0,-0x18(%rbp) ; je 30      <- false arm, edge 1
       16:  mov -0x18(%rbp),%rax ; add $0x4,%rax ; mov (%rax),%eax
       20:  and $0x100,%eax ; test %eax,%eax ; je 30   <- false arm, edge 2
       29:  mov $0x1,%eax ; jmp 35
       30:  mov $0x0,%eax                      <- TWO in-edges
       35:  mov %eax,-0x4(%rbp)                <- the MULTIEQUAL

    Root cause (P3, upstream-faithful).  RuleConditionalMove is the rule that
    folds MULTIEQUAL(0,1) into zext(cond)/BOOL_AND/BOOL_OR, and it fires on the
    one-test shape, but it requires each MULTIEQUAL input block to be the
    CBRANCH root itself or a SINGLE-predecessor pass-through (upstream Ghidra
    ruleaction.cc:9427, `if (inblock->sizeIn() != 1) return 0;`).  The short-circuit
    chain gives the constant arm two predecessors, so it bails, and the bail is
    correct at the IR level: no single dominating CBRANCH stands for the whole
    chain, and hoisting `p[1]` out of its `p != 0` guard would evaluate it
    unconditionally.  So the re-roll can only be done AFTER structuring, where the
    chain is already one BlockCondition that C's own `&&` renders with
    short-circuit semantics.

    Stage model: P8 "goto-quality" (S8 structured-tree rewrite), rendered in P9.
    The P0 assertion `option iteboolean on|off` selects it; the pass is
    print-only (it marks the condition's terminal CBRANCH, mutates no p-code).

    Pass 1 (option iteboolean off) reproduces the gap: the explicit two-arm
    constant diamond `if (...) v1 = 1; else v1 = 0;`.
    Pass 2 (option iteboolean on, the default) proves the fix: one boolean
    assignment `v1 = ((a0) && (...));` with the short-circuit condition intact.
-->
